/F2 11 Tf`n([ABSTRACT]) Tj
0 -14 Td
/F1 10 Tf`n(Organizations hold private documents in English and regional languages across PDFs, DOCX) Tj
0 -14 Td
(files, and scanned images. Keyword search misses semantically related passages, while) Tj
0 -14 Td
(general-purpose language models can provide unsupported answers. This project develops and) Tj
0 -14 Td
(evaluates a multilingual Retrieval-Augmented Generation system that retrieves evidence from) Tj
0 -14 Td
(private document libraries and produces answers with page-level citations. The central study) Tj
0 -14 Td
(compares direct multilingual embeddings, translation-to-English embeddings, and an adaptive) Tj
0 -14 Td
(hybrid retrieval route. The system combines OCR-aware ingestion, semantic and lexical) Tj
0 -14 Td
(search, cross-encoder reranking, a lightweight answer generator, and abstention when) Tj
0 -14 Td
(evidence is insufficient. The intended contribution is a reproducible evaluation of) Tj
0 -14 Td
(retrieval accuracy, citation faithfulness, language fidelity, OCR robustness, latency, and) Tj
0 -14 Td
(resource cost for English and selected Indian languages.) Tj
0 -14 Td
() Tj
0 -14 Td
/F2 11 Tf`n([PROBLEM STATEMENT]) Tj
0 -14 Td
/F1 10 Tf`n(Existing multilingual RAG research usually concentrates on one dimension: translation, a) Tj
0 -14 Td
(single low-resource language, multimodal retrieval, or a narrow legal corpus. There remains) Tj
0 -14 Td
(insufficient evidence on how to build a trustworthy and resource-efficient system for) Tj
0 -14 Td
(heterogeneous private documents in English and Indian languages, especially when source) Tj
0 -14 Td
(citations, OCR noise, language consistency, and constrained hardware are important.) Tj
0 -14 Td
() Tj
0 -14 Td
/F2 11 Tf`n([AIM]) Tj
0 -14 Td
/F1 10 Tf`n(To design and evaluate a citation-grounded multilingual RAG system for private document) Tj
0 -14 Td
(collections that selects or combines retrieval strategies according to language, query, and) Tj
0 -14 Td
(document characteristics.) Tj
0 -14 Td
() Tj
0 -14 Td
/F2 11 Tf`n([OBJECTIVES]) Tj
0 -14 Td
/F1 10 Tf`n(1. Ingest native PDFs, DOCX files, and scanned documents through parsing, OCR, language) Tj
0 -14 Td
(identification, and page-aware chunking.) Tj
0 -14 Td
(2. Compare direct multilingual embedding, translation-based embedding, and hybrid) Tj
0 -14 Td
(dense-plus-BM25 retrieval.) Tj
0 -14 Td
(3. Improve ranking using a multilingual cross-encoder reranker.) Tj
0 -14 Td
(4. Generate concise answers with page-level document citations and an explicit) Tj
0 -14 Td
(insufficient-evidence response.) Tj
0 -14 Td
(5. Evaluate retrieval quality, faithfulness, answer-language fidelity, latency, and resource) Tj
0 -14 Td
(use for English and selected Indian languages.) Tj
0 -14 Td
() Tj
0 -14 Td
/F2 11 Tf`n([PROPOSED METHODOLOGY]) Tj
0 -14 Td
/F1 10 Tf`n(Ingestion: Extract text and metadata from PDF/DOCX; use Tesseract OCR for scans; detect) Tj
0 -14 Td
(language; split text into overlapping, page-preserving chunks.) Tj
0 -14 Td
(Indexing: Store chunk text, language, document ID, page number, and embeddings in PostgreSQL) Tj
0 -14 Td
(with pgvector HNSW. Maintain BM25 lexical retrieval alongside dense retrieval.) Tj
0 -14 Td
(Retrieval experiment: Run three conditions: \(A\) multilingual-E5 direct retrieval, \(B\)) Tj
0 -14 Td
(query/document translation followed by English embedding, and \(C\) hybrid dense-plus-BM25) Tj
0 -14 Td
(retrieval with cross-encoder reranking. An adaptive router may select the route based on) Tj
